\(CK\\) from vertex \\(C\\) to the base \\(AD\\). \n   - This makes \\(CK = 8\\).\n\n3. **Calculate Bases' Segment Differentiation**:\n   - Calculate segment \\(KD\\) in terms of \\(AD\\) and \\(BC\\):\n     \\[\n     KD = \\frac{AD - BC}{2} = \\frac{21 - 9}{2} = 6\n     \\]\n\n4. **Apply the Pythagorean Theorem**:\n   - Calculate the length of the lateral side \\(CD\\) using the Pythagorean theorem:\n     \\[\n     CD = \\sqrt{CK^2 + KD^2} = \\sqrt{8^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 36} = \\sqrt{100} = 10\n     \\]\n\n5. **Calculate Sine of Angle**:\n   - Calculate the sine of angle \\(\\angle D\\) in triangle \\(CDK\\):\n     \\[\n     \\sin \\angle D = \\frac{CK}{CD} = \\frac{8}{10} = \\frac{4}{5}\n     \\]\n\n6. **Calculate Diagonal AC**:\n   - Use the Pythagorean theorem to calculate the length of diagonal \\(AC\\):\n     \\[\n     AK = \\sqrt{AD - KD - KD'} = \\sqrt{21 - 6 - 6} = \\sqrt{21-12} = \\sqrt{9} = \\sqrt{15^2 + 8^2} = 17\n     \\]\n\n7. **Calculate Radius \\(R\\)**:\n   - Using the formula for the radius of the circumcircle around the isosceles trapezoid:\n     \\[\n     R = \\frac{AC}{2 \\sin \\angle D} = \\frac{17}{2 \\sin \\left( \\frac{4}{5} \\right)} = \\frac{17}{2 \\cdot \\frac{4}{5}} = \\frac{17 \\cdot 5}{8} = \\frac{85}{8}\n     \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{85}{8}}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Given two linear functions \\( f(x) \\) and \\( g(x) \\) such that the graphs \\( y = f(x) \\) and \\( y = g(x) \\) are parallel lines that are not parallel to the coordinate axes. Find the minimum value of the function \\( 3(g(x))^2 + 2 f(x) \\), given that the minimum value of the function \\( 3(f(x))^2 + 2 g(x) \\) is \\( -\\frac{19}{6} \\).", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, so I need to find the minimum value of the function \\( 3(g(x))^2 + 2 f(x) \\), given that the minimum value of \\( 3(f(x))^2 + 2 g(x) \\) is \\( -\\frac{19}{6} \\). Both \\( f(x) \\) and \\( g(x) \\) 